Configuring Storage Backends
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Understand the importance of persistent storage backends for HashiCorp Vault
Configure Vault with Consul storage backend for high availability
Set up Vault with file-based storage backend for development environments
Compare different storage backend options and their use cases
Implement proper security configurations for storage backends
Verify storage backend functionality through practical testing
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with text editors (nano, vim, or similar)
Knowledge of basic networking concepts
Understanding of JSON configuration files
Previous experience with HashiCorp Vault basics (recommended)
Lab Environment Setup
Note: Al Nafi provides Linux-based cloud machines for this lab. Simply click "Start Lab" to access your dedicated Linux machine. The provided machine is bare metal with no pre-installed tools, so you will install all required software during the lab exercises.

