Task 2: Configure File-Based Storage Backend
Subtask 2.1: Create File Storage Configuration
Create a basic Vault configuration using file storage:

# Create configuration directory
mkdir -p ~/vault-lab/config

# Create file storage configuration
cat > ~/vault-lab/config/vault-file.hcl << 'EOF'
# Vault configuration with file storage backend
storage "file" {
  path = "/opt/vault/data"
}

listener "tcp" {
  address     = "127.0.0.1:8200"
  tls_disable = 1
}

api_addr = "http://127.0.0.1:8200"
cluster_addr = "https://127.0.0.1:8201"
ui = true

# Disable mlock for development
disable_mlock = true
EOF
Subtask 2.2: Prepare File Storage Directory
Set up the storage directory with proper permissions:

# Create storage directory
sudo mkdir -p /opt/vault/data

# Set proper ownership and permissions
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER /opt/vault
chmod 755 /opt/vault
chmod 700 /opt/vault/data
Subtask 2.3: Start Vault with File Storage
Initialize and start Vault with file storage:

# Start Vault server in background
vault server -config=~/vault-lab/config/vault-file.hcl > ~/vault-lab/vault-file.log 2>&1 &

# Wait for server to start
sleep 5

# Set environment variable
export VAULT_ADDR='http://127.0.0.1:8200'

# Check server status
vault status
Subtask 2.4: Initialize and Unseal Vault
Initialize the Vault and save the keys:

# Initialize Vault
vault operator init -key-shares=5 -key-threshold=3 > ~/vault-lab/vault-keys.txt

# Display the keys (save these securely in production)
cat ~/vault-lab/vault-keys.txt

# Extract unseal keys and root token
UNSEAL_KEY_1=$(grep 'Unseal Key 1:' ~/vault-lab/vault-keys.txt | awk '{print $4}')
UNSEAL_KEY_2=$(grep 'Unseal Key 2:' ~/vault-lab/vault-keys.txt | awk '{print $4}')
UNSEAL_KEY_3=$(grep 'Unseal Key 3:' ~/vault-lab/vault-keys.txt | awk '{print $4}')
ROOT_TOKEN=$(grep 'Initial Root Token:' ~/vault-lab/vault-keys.txt | awk '{print $4}')

# Unseal Vault
vault operator unseal $UNSEAL_KEY_1
vault operator unseal $UNSEAL_KEY_2
vault operator unseal $UNSEAL_KEY_3

# Authenticate with root token
vault auth $ROOT_TOKEN
Subtask 2.5: Test File Storage Backend
Verify that data is being stored in the file system:

# Enable KV secrets engine
vault secrets enable -path=secret kv-v2

# Store a test secret
vault kv put secret/test-file username="fileuser" password="filepass123"

# Verify secret storage
vault kv get secret/test-file

# Check physical storage
ls -la /opt/vault/data/
find /opt/vault/data/ -type f | head -10
Subtask 2.6: Stop File Storage Vault
Stop the current Vault instance:

